{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"15502a7e0f5e3db5333673ba254f56c07933d32f9fd000d351cfb7c650eca766","packTokens":4631,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"platform","tokens":215,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":627,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":1510,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":2173,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"PLATFORM. This product is designed and built as a web app, and nothing else. Where the requirements ask for a mobile app, a phone app, an iOS or Android app, treat them as the same features in one responsive web app that works well on a phone's browser: never stop, park, ask or leave a requirement out because it names a mobile app, and never plan a native app, an app store step or a phone-only frame. Every page is responsive: it is laid out for a phone, a tablet and a desktop width, with touch-sized controls on the narrow one. What only a native app can do (push notifications, background location, a home-screen icon) is given its closest web form (an in-app notice or email, the browser's location prompt, an installable web app) and said so.\n\nMap each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Replace the current manual processes with a single platform covering stock, orders, deliveries, live temperature monitoring, quality decisions and recalls.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide a responsive web portal for warehouse staff, dispatchers, quality staff, administrators and auditors.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide a customer portal for hospitals, pharmacies and clinics.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide a driver experience that keeps working without a connection.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Receive temperature readings from data loggers and cold-room sensors.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Keep a centralized shared record of stock, orders and temperature history.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-7\",\n  \"text\": \"Support secure sign-in, role and warehouse access controls, customer-organization isolation, and read-only auditor access.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-8\",\n  \"text\": \"Define versioned product temperature profiles and stability budgets.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-9\",\n  \"text\": \"Receive stock by lot, track inbound logger readings, quarantine stock, and release it through quality review.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-10\",\n  \"text\": \"Let customer users place, view, change and cancel orders under the specified delivery and order rules.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-11\",\n  \"text\": \"Allocate released stock to orders by earliest expiry while respecting shelf-life, availability and order-completion rules.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-12\",\n  \"text\": \"Pack stock into qualified shipper boxes and plan routes with drivers and vehicles.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-13\",\n  \"text\": \"Store and process delayed, duplicated and out-of-order temperature readings reliably.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-14\",\n  \"text\": \"Detect excursions, charge stability budgets, place affected stock on hold, and alert relevant users.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-15\",\n  \"text\": \"Enable drivers to load, drive and record delivery handovers using their phone, including offline use.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-16\",\n  \"text\": \"Support the portals in English and Arabic, with Arabic displayed right to left.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-17\",\n  \"text\": \"Track recalled lots, block remaining stock and account for customer responses.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"What must the full two-person quality decision for stock exposed to a not-permitted temperature range require?\",\n  \"answer\": \"A Quality Officer proposes the disposition and a different Quality Manager approves it; neither person can perform both steps.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"When an excursion opens, how quickly must affected stock be placed On Hold relative to the alert deadline?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Place it On Hold as soon as the excursion is detected; the two-minute deadline applies to alerts.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"What customer evidence must the driver record for a delivery handover?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Record the recipient's name and an explicit electronic acknowledgment of receipt; a drawn signature is not required.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"What should happen to quantities that are not handed over because a delivery is refused or only partly completed?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Keep undelivered quantities outstanding; record the reason and return them to available stock only after warehouse receipt and any required quality checks.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"What constitutes a handling unit for tracking stability budgets when a received quantity is split, moved, or packed into different boxes?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Track quantities as handling units and split the record whenever portions acquire different temperature histories.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Who may maintain a customer organisation's saved delivery addresses and minimum remaining shelf-life requirement?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Customer Administrators maintain their organisation's addresses; System Administrators set its minimum shelf life.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"How should the stock quantity breakdown reconcile with quantity on hand, given that stock can also be On Hold, Rejected, Recalled or Expired?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Treat on-hand as the total and show a mutually exclusive breakdown that includes available, allocated, quarantined and the other stock statuses.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"When a product profile changes with an effective date, how should the new profile affect stock already received and its temperature-budget history?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Apply the new version to stock still held from its effective date onward and recalculate affected budgets and decisions from that date.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Yes: \\\"The system shall be sized for 5,000 devices reporting at once.\\\"\",\n  \"by\": \"factory\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-13\",\n  \"question\": \"Does the request ask for this: Support the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox, and support the stated first-year user and record volume and simultaneous device volume.\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Split the full scope across about four runs; keep all requirements.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-9\",\n  \"question\": \"The 28 requirements are estimated at about four runs of work. How would you like the scope handled?\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Retain unsynchronized actions in a queue tied to the originating driver; sync only after that same driver signs in again, and erase or reject the queue if access is refused or the account is disabled.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-10\",\n  \"question\": \"What should happen to unsynchronized driver actions when a driver signs out or the API reports the account disabled, especially if another user later signs in on the same browser?\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Flag the gap for review and show the API-returned stock status; do not automatically place the stock On Hold.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-11\",\n  \"question\": \"When a temperature-history gap affects stock, should the stock be automatically placed On Hold while the gap is unresolved, or should the gap be flagged for review without automatically changing stock status?\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Require effective dates to be today or later; do not recalculate earlier decisions.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-12\",\n  \"question\": \"May a temperature-profile version have an effective date in the past, and if so, how should recalculated results affect stock that was already released or had a quality decision?\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-14\",\n  \"question\": \"If an offline handover is queued and the API returns a restriction because the stock went On Hold or was recalled, how should the app handle that recorded handover?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Do not mark the delivery as completed; show the returned restriction and leave the affected quantity outstanding for follow-up.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-15\",\n  \"question\": \"Q-10 settles that queued actions stay tied to the originating driver across sign-out and workday end, and are erased or rejected if access is refused or the account is disabled. Should any additional local protection or expiry rule apply to queued actions containing recipient names on a shared browser?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Keep the existing same-driver access rule and retain queued actions until sync or API rejection/refusal; add no local encryption or expiry.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Provide a responsive Meridian web app with role-oriented portal pages and navigation for stock, orders, deliveries, temperature monitoring, quality decisions, and recalls across phone, tablet, and desktop widths.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Provide staff sign-in through Meridian Microsoft accounts and customer sign-in using email, password, and a one-time code, plus password-reset links by email; do not offer social sign-in or single sign-on for customer accounts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Show users only records and actions returned for their roles, assigned warehouses, and customer organisations; keep Auditor views read-only and clear protected data when access is refused.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Allow Customer Administrators to invite and remove users within their own organisation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Allow System Administrators to list, search, view, deactivate, and maintain products, and create versioned temperature profiles with storage bands, contiguous non-overlapping tiers, allowances or not-permitted designations, a reason, and an effective date no earlier than today; keep earlier versions read-only.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"When a temperature-profile version takes effect, show the new version and API-returned recalculated budgets, decisions, and statuses for stock still held from its effective date onward; keep earlier decisions unchanged and show returned order, box, and route outcomes for affected allocated or packed stock.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Allow Warehouse Operators to record receipts with product, lot number, expiry date, quantity, supplier, and storage location, and show returned quarantine status and inbound temperature information before release.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Provide inbound logger-file upload and display returned temperature history and budget use; validate separate receipt-evidence image or PDF files and accept logger exports in the supplier's documented format.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Present available quality release or disposition actions and API-returned decision states, including separate proposal and approval steps for not-permitted-range dispositions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Show on-hand stock with mutually exclusive quantities for available, allocated, quarantined, On Hold, Rejected, Recalled, and Expired statuses, plus returned warehouse, lot, product, receipt, and location details.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Show portions of received stock with different temperature histories as separate handling units with their returned quantities, histories, and tier-budget use and remaining.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"Provide stock-movement forms and show the returned movement record with source and destination locations, quantity, actor, and time.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"Allow Customer Administrators to maintain their organisation's saved delivery addresses and System Administrators to set the organisation's minimum remaining shelf-life requirement; show that value read-only to customer users and Dispatchers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"Allow customer users to create orders with one or more product lines, pack quantities, a saved delivery address, an eligible delivery date, and a choice between delivery of available quantities and complete delivery only.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"Show order status and allocated and outstanding quantities per line; provide customer change and cancellation controls only before Packed, expose dispatcher cancellation controls when returned as available, and display API outcomes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"Show order allocations by line and lot, including returned expiry dates and quantities; provide dispatcher lot-override controls with a required reason and API outcome, and show returned allocation and stock-status outcomes in order, box, and route views.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"Allow Warehouse Operators to pack stock into shipper boxes by type, associate one logger with each box, and show compatibility, contents, and sealing details returned by the API.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"Allow Dispatchers to create and view routes with a date, vehicle, driver, ordered stops, and planned arrival times; show route-confirmation errors and confirmed-route changes returned by the API, including configured qualified-duration safety margins.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"Show temperature histories for boxes, cold rooms, and lots as charts and tables with returned readings, applicable bands, excursions, gaps, and reading flags or silence status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"Show excursions, handling-unit budget use and remaining allowances, returned alerts, and returned hold and decision statuses for affected devices and stock.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"For unresolved temperature-history gaps, show the returned gap, review status, stock status, and budget values without inferring an On Hold status, estimating a temperature tier, or presenting an estimated charge to an unobserved tier.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"Show the returned quality-review case to relevant customer and staff users when corrected temperature history identifies an excursion affecting stock already delivered.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 23,\n  \"text\": \"Provide an installable, responsive driver web experience that caches the current workday's assigned route, queues supported loading and delivery actions for synchronization when connectivity returns, and retains unsynchronized actions tied to the originating driver until synchronization succeeds or the API rejects or refuses them.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 24,\n  \"text\": \"Synchronize queued driver actions only after the same driver signs in again; clear cached route and delivery data when the driver signs out, the workday ends, or access is refused, and erase or mark queued actions rejected when access is refused or the account is disabled.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 25,\n  \"text\": \"Show returned stale-route and queued-action outcomes, and do not expose the originating driver's route, recipient details, or queued-action details to another user or send synchronization requests for that driver's actions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 26,\n  \"text\": \"When a driver records a delivery handover, capture the recipient's name, explicit electronic acknowledgment, quantities handed over, and any refusal or partial-delivery reason; show outstanding quantities and returned delivery status, including restrictions returned when an offline handover synchronizes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 27,\n  \"text\": \"Allow Quality Managers to start recalls by selecting affected lots and providing a reason, view and manage recall records, and close recalls; allow customer users to submit a quantity and stated disposition for each affected delivery and show returned reconciliation and stock-block information.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 28,\n  \"text\": \"Provide filtered on-screen operational lists and CSV export, and show creator and last-changer identities and timestamps as read-only metadata where returned.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 29,\n  \"text\": \"Provide English and Arabic portal content, rendering Arabic pages right to left and English pages left to right.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 30,\n  \"text\": \"Ensure every portal page reflows for phone, tablet, and desktop browser widths, with touch-sized controls on narrow layouts; conform the main staff, customer, and driver web flows to WCAG 2.1 Level AA.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 31,\n  \"text\": \"Support the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox, and support the stated first-year user and record volume while displaying data from the stated simultaneous device volume.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}